 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Email is lovely, but a quick team chat also works. Keep it short and only include people whose phone rings. Then tell her to stop asking, you' not her maid of honor. If she push, tell her the wedding is small and intimate, that's all. Then apologize and say you're exclusive. If she doesn't accept that, she wasn't your friend to start with. You do, of course. Just keep it simple. Go somewhere the couple doesn't go right away, like a nice pub that's still open at midnight. People will still be talking in morning. Good. Also, think about including a friend of hers who would make a good wingman. He can stand up for her if she starts getting upset.",
